# sriq: SELF. A is r-related to itself; whatever has an r-successor in B is a C.
# So D ≡ A ⊓ B, its own r-successor being in B, is a C.
# Expect: D ⊑ C.

@prefix :     <http://example.org/t#> .
@prefix owl:  <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .

<http://example.org/t> a owl:Ontology .
:A a owl:Class . :B a owl:Class . :C a owl:Class . :D a owl:Class .
:r a owl:ObjectProperty .
:A rdfs:subClassOf [ a owl:Restriction ; owl:onProperty :r ; owl:hasSelf true ] .
[ a owl:Restriction ; owl:onProperty :r ; owl:someValuesFrom :B ] rdfs:subClassOf :C .
:D owl:equivalentClass [ owl:intersectionOf ( :A :B ) ] .
